<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan awards one Jan-Jun'97 gas oil, mulls second.</title>
<headline>Taiwan awards one Jan-Jun'97 gas oil, mulls second.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp has awarded one six-month term contract to sell gas oil and is negotiating to award a second contract, a company source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender to sell four to six cargoes of 225,000-250,000 barrels of 0.3 percent sulphur gas oil each was awarded at a 50 cents premium to spot Singapore quotes on a free-on-board Kaoshiung basis, the source said.</p>
<p>The tender closed on December 10 and offers are valid to December 13.</p>
<p>Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
